  Fallback only — the real, up-to-date sitemap is generated at build time
  by scripts/generate-sitemap.mjs (npm's "postbuild" step, see
  package.json) into dist/sitemap.xml, which also adds every live
  approved publisher profile and channel page from the database. This
  file is what ships only if that step never runs (e.g. the build
  pipeline fails before reaching postbuild) — kept reasonably complete
  and current by hand as a fallback, not authoritative. If you're editing
  routes, update STATIC_ROUTES in that script; this file will drift from
  it over time and that's an accepted trade-off for a fallback, not a bug
  to keep chasing.

  "claude to fix 2" item 25 — this list used to cover only 13 fixed
  routes; audited against every <Route> in src/App.tsx and brought up to
  the same 61 public, indexable static routes the generator script uses
  (still none of the dynamic publisher/channel/article URLs, which need a
  live database or the generator's source-file parsing to enumerate —
  see that script for why this file alone can't include them).

  Update the domain below if it ever changes — currently the real domain
  (chatsched.com), matching robots.txt and the rest of the codebase.
-->
